.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="The Van Vleck-Morette semiclassical propagator (/api/gallery/semiclassical/propagators/plot_semiclassical_propagators) needs a topological correction beyond its classical action and stability prefactor: every time a classical trajectory crosses a caustic (a focal point where \partial q_t/\partial p_0=0), the propagator picks up an extra phase of -\pi/2. Joseph Keller&#x27;s corrected Bohr-Sommerfeld (EBK) quantization condition built exactly this caustic-counting correction into the old quantum theory, and Viktor Maslov later showed that the resulting phase count -- the Maslov index \mu -- is a topological invariant of the trajectory itself, rather than an artifact of the coordinates used to compute it.">

.. only:: html

  .. image:: /api/gallery/semiclassical/propagators/images/thumb/sphx_glr_plot_maslov_index_caustics_thumb.png
    :alt:

  :doc:`/api/gallery/semiclassical/propagators/plot_maslov_index_caustics`

.. raw:: html

      <div class="sphx-glr-thumbnail-title">The Maslov index: caustics and Keller's quantization condition</div>
    </div>


